# Generated files that are nevertheless committed.
#
# The five esbuild bundles are NOT here — they are gitignored, built with
# `npm run build`. These two are different: web/i18n.js is the base that
# scripts/i18n-merge.mjs reads, merges into and writes back, so it cannot be
# regenerated from i18n.patch.json alone; web/i18n.stamp.json is the English
# baseline scripts/i18n-check.mjs compares against. Both are input as much as
# output, and both are large.
#
# linguist-generated collapses them in pull-request diffs and keeps them out of
# GitHub's language statistics.
#
# eol=lf is not cosmetic here, and it was learned the hard way. Every page
# carries a content hash of i18n.js written by scripts/stamp-assets.mjs. The
# file is produced with LF and stored with LF, but on Windows git checks it out
# with CRLF by default — different bytes, different hash. A fresh clone
# therefore re-stamped all six pages before a single test ran, and the promise
# that a clone reproduces what is committed held only on the machine that made
# it. Pinned to LF, the hash is the same everywhere.

web/i18n.js         text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
web/i18n.stamp.json text eol=lf linguist-generated=true

# web/i18n.patch.json is NOT listed as generated: it is the hand-edited input,
# and its diffs are the ones worth reading. It is pinned to LF all the same,
# because i18n-merge.mjs reads it and a stray CR would travel into a string.
web/i18n.patch.json text eol=lf
